# The build context of the Dockerfile at the root, as an allowlist: everything
# is left out, and what the build compiles is named back in. A COPY of a path
# this file leaves out fails only when the image is next built, after the
# gates, so the `build-context` gate holds every COPY source to this file.
# Name a path back in with a comment saying what reads it, and never by a
# wildcard family.
*

# The Rust workspace: its manifests, its lock, its configuration, the pinned
# toolchain and the crates.
!/Cargo.toml
!/Cargo.lock
!/.cargo
!/rust-toolchain.toml
!/crates

# What a build leaves behind never enters the context.
**/target
